# shellcheck shell=bash
# nix-direnv is recommended for evaluation caching only. It is NOT required for
# GC safety: direnv's own `use_flake` runs `nix print-dev-env --profile
# "$(direnv_layout_dir)/flake-profile"`, and a Nix profile generation is a
# permanent GC root (`createGeneration` -> `addPermRoot`), so the devShell's
# store paths survive `nix-collect-garbage` with or without nix-direnv. Do not
# add a `nix_direnv_version` probe to solve a problem that does not exist.
#
# Interactive shells enter the devShell on `cd`, after a one-time `direnv
# allow`. Non-interactive contexts — CI, agents, editor tasks, `bash -c` — do
# not fire the prompt hook and must wrap commands explicitly:
#     nix develop --command prek run --all-files
#     direnv exec . <cmd>
use flake

# The workspace builds the `exobrain` CLI into target/debug, and this
# repository runs its own build rather than a released pin.
PATH_add target/debug

# Developer-specific values, such as the release-bot App ID and the path of its
# private key, live in .envrc.local, which git ignores. .envrc.local.example is
# the tracked template.
source_env_if_exists .envrc.local

# Keep the sdd pin fresh: at most one bump a day per checkout, silent when
# there is nothing to do, leaving a two-file diff to review when the pin moved.
# The default caller is `envrc`, which stays silent and exits 0.
sdd self-depend sync --apply || true

# Keep the release-kit pin fresh the same way: at most once a day, leaving the
# flake.nix and flake.lock diff to review and commit.
rk self-depend sync --apply || true

# Report a store copy of this checkout once a day: a flake reference that does
# not read the git tree copies the whole tree into the Nix store
# (project-platform:a-flake-is-read-from-its-git-tree). A fresh checkout with no
# build skips the guard until `just build` runs.
if command -v exobrain >/dev/null 2>&1; then exobrain store-guard --daily || true; fi
